        <figcaption>Explore. The whole plan as a tree, and every task with its spec, its checks, and its history.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Team -->
<section class="sec" id="team">
  <div class="leg">
    <div class="lane" style="--dx:30px"><svg class="sym wp"><use href="#s-agent"/></svg><p class="lbl"><span class="who">One crew</span></p></div>
    <div class="txt">
      <h2>One plan for the whole crew.</h2>
      <p>Agent work tends to live in one person's chat window. Tiller moves the plan, the decisions, and the state into the repo, where every person and every agent on the project reads the same thing.</p>
      <p class="how-h">How Tiller does it</p>
      <ul class="how">
        <li><a href={url("concepts/#where-things-live")}>Plain files in git</a><p>Markdown for what you want, YAML for where it stands. No database and no hosted service, so cloning the repo clones the plan.</p></li>
        <li><a href={url("skills/")}>Bring any agent</a><p>Tiller serves its skills to any harness through <code>tiller guide</code>, so everyone sees the same instructions.</p></li>
        <li><a href={url("console/#explore")}>Questions that hold the work</a><p>When something needs an answer, it's written down and the work it blocks waits for it, instead of getting lost in a thread.</p></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="crew" aria-label="Agents that work with Tiller">
        <li>Claude Code</li><li>Codex</li><li>Pi</li><li>a plain shell</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="inset art">
      <span class="inset-t">The plan, in your repo</span>
<pre>.tiller/epics/event-night/
  epic.md                  <span class="h">yours:</span> intent
  epic.yml                 <i>Tiller's:</i> state
  features/door-check-in/
    feature.md             the spec
    feature.eval.md        acceptance criteria
    feature.yml            status, gates
    tasks/attendee-search/
      task.md
      task.yml</pre>
      <figcaption>Versioned right alongside the code it describes.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- How it fits together -->
<section class="sec" id="how">
  <div class="leg wide">
    <div class="lane" style="--dx:12px"><svg class="sym wp"><use href="#s-wp"/></svg><p class="lbl"><span class="who">The passage</span></p></div>
    <div class="txt">
      <h2>How it fits together</h2>
      <p class="sub">Your agent does the thinking and the typing. You make the calls at each step. Tiller holds the plan, the checks, and the state in between.</p>
