      <h2>Everything Tiller can do</h2>
      <p class="sub">One binary with 44 commands, a local console, and eleven agent skills. Here's the lay of the land, and where to read more.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="full">
      <div class="idx-wrap">
        <ul class="idx">
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#the-tree")}><span class="t">Plan the work</span><span class="s">An agent proposes epics and features from your design docs, and you approve the shape.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#the-lifecycle-and-its-gates")}><span class="t">Specify just in time</span><span class="s">Spec, acceptance criteria, and tasks for one feature, when its turn comes.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#gates-and-evidence")}><span class="t">Gates and evidence</span><span class="s">Required checks that block done, plus optional review attestations.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#review-grain")}><span class="t">Review grain</span><span class="s">Review by task, feature, or epic, set per project, epic, or feature.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#contributors-and-claims")}><span class="t">Claims and contributors</span><span class="s">Who's on what, how work changes hands, and what happens when it has to.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#bugs-chores-and-tweaks")}><span class="t">Bugs, chores, and tweaks</span><span class="s">Unplanned work gets captured, triaged by a person, and run like any other task.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#corrections-drift-and-amendments")}><span class="t">Drift and amendments</span><span class="s">Change the plan on purpose, with a reviewed amendment, and catch it when it changes by accident.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href={url("concepts/#existing-code-baseline")}><span class="t">Existing codebases</span><span class="s">Start from code you already have. The agent writes down what it does today, and you confirm it.</span></a></li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="idx">
          <li><a href={url("console/#home-the-desk")}><span class="t">Home</span><span class="s">The desk: what needs you, what's moving, what just happened.</span></a></li>
